## Original Content
A press conference marking the 103rd anniversary of the massacre following the 1923 Great Kanto Earthquake was held in Tokyo on Friday, with participants calling for Japan to confront its history and avoid repeating the mistakes of the past.

## Summary
Activists held a press conference in Tokyo to mark the 103rd anniversary of the massacre following the 1923 Great Kanto Earthquake, urging Japan to confront its history and avoid repeating past mistakes.

## Key Points
- A press conference commemorated the 103rd anniversary of the massacre from the 1923 Great Kanto Earthquake.
- The event took place in Tokyo on a Friday.
- Participants, including activists, called for Japan to confront historical events.
- The aim is to prevent repetition of atrocities by learning from the past.
- This highlights ongoing efforts to acknowledge and address historical incidents.


